---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site.ts';
---

<Base
  title="About PowerStation Size"
  description="What PowerStation Size is, how the calculator and spec library work, how the site is funded, and how to send a correction."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">About {site.name}</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-500 dark:text-ink-400">{site.domain}</p>

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      {site.name} is a free calculator and a library of manufacturer specifications for portable
      power stations. The job of the site is to answer how much capacity you need, whether the
      inverter can hold the running watts, and whether a published peak will start a motor. It is
      not a ranked review list and it is not a store.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Why the site exists</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Most sizing pages answer a different question. They tell you which product is best in a
      category. The question people actually type is closer to: will this run a fridge through an
      outage, or a CPAP through a night, and how many watt-hours should I shop for.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Those are two checks, not one. A station can hold enough energy and still refuse to start a
      compressor. A CPAP with a heated humidifier can draw roughly twice the power of the same
      machine running dry. Combining those into one default would give an answer that is wrong in
      the direction that matters.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What you can do here</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        <a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href="/calculator/">The calculator</a>
        takes the devices you run. Capacity, continuous watts, and startup surge are checked
        separately. Hours update as you type. You can copy a link that encodes the load in the URL.
      </li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        <a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href="/scenarios/">Worked scenarios</a>
        (CPAP night, fridge outage, camping day, a power tool) show the estimated watt-hours and
        which published nameplates cover that load.
      </li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        <a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href="/stations/">Station pages</a>
        list capacity, continuous output, and peak, with the manufacturer URL and the date those
        figures were read. A peak that is only a resistive boost is labeled so it is not used as
        inverter surge.
      </li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        <a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href="/guides/">Guides</a>
        include decision pages for
        <a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href="/guides/cpap-backup-power/">CPAP backup</a>
        and
        <a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href="/guides/camping-power-station/">camping</a>,
        plus watts versus watt-hours and surge versus boost.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">How the numbers are made</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Each station record is copied from the manufacturer product page named on that record:
      capacity, continuous output, and the peak figure, plus the date that page was read. If the
      only peak on the page is a resistive boost, the record is marked so the calculator will not
      use it to clear a motor start. Runtime hours are calculated from those figures and from the
      device library. They are not lab measurements. This site does not claim to have tested the
      machines overnight.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Device wattages are typical ranges. Where a manufacturer publishes a figure, that is noted on
      the device entry. Where it does not, the range is an engineering estimate used to seed the
      calculator. You can edit watts and hours on every row.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Default constants: inverter efficiency 0.85, reserve margin 1.20, usable capacity 0.85. The
      formulas, the solar check, and the known limitations are on the
      <a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.
      A verification older than 90 days is flagged on the model page.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Who publishes this site</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      {site.name} is published by {site.publisherName}. It is a specification library and
      calculator, not a lab and not a medical publisher. Station numbers are transcribed from the
      manufacturer page named on each record. Runtime hours are calculated from those figures and
      from the device library. This site does not claim hands-on overnight testing.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Source for the calculator and the specification database is on
      <a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href="https://github.com/rosebsnowden-eng/powerstation-size" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
      Corrections go to
      <!--email_off--><a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a><!--/email_off-->.
      Send the model name and the manufacturer page that contradicts the record.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">How it is funded</h2>
    {
      site.affiliateLive ? (
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
          The site is supported by affiliate commissions. If you follow a link to a retailer and buy
          something, we may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. That never changes what the
          calculator recommends. See the
          <a class="underline" href="/disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
          There are no retailer checkout links on this site. Hosting is static. If an affiliate
          program later approves the site, commissions may support the work, and the
          <a class="underline" href="/disclosure/">disclosure page</a> will name the program in the
          same deploy as the links. Commissions will not change calculator output or which models
          appear.
        </p>
      )
    }
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      We do not accept payment for placement. We do not run price-tracking or price-drop alerts.
      Manufacturer list prices, where available, are dated reference figures, not live offers.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What this site is not</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        It is not medical advice. A power station is not a medical device and is not a substitute
        for the battery your equipment maker specifies. Confirm a therapy backup plan with your
        provider and your clinician.
      </li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        It is not electrical advice. Never backfeed household wiring through a wall or dryer
        outlet. Whole-home backup needs a manufacturer-approved, code-compliant transfer or isolation
        system, installed by a qualified electrician where required.
      </li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        It is not a review site with hands-on testing. Every runtime figure is calculated from
        published specifications.
      </li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        It is not the manufacturer. Brand names and packshots identify products. They are not an
        endorsement by those companies.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Contact and corrections</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Email
      <!--email_off--><a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a><!--/email_off-->.
      If a specification is wrong, send the model name and the manufacturer page that contradicts
      us. That is the most serious error this site can make. The record will be corrected and the
      verification date updated.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Privacy practices are on the
      <a class="underline" href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
      Rules for using the estimates are on the
      <a class="underline" href="/terms/">terms of use</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
